But Eric!

I taught my kitten to fetch about three months ago, and now that she's
grown, I can toss her favorite ball of paper the length of the house and
she's off like a kangaroo, bounce, bounce, bounce, and has it back to me
within 20 seconds if she saw where it went, and within fifteen minutes if
she has to hunt it down.

Cats are very good at "fetch", you just have to start with something they
can carry easily (a wadded up 3x5 card is ideal), start with short fetches
(three feet or so), and reward them lavishly with praise and petting when
they get the object back to you.  It works just like the game; reward them
for dropping it at your feet, even if it was by accident, and the next time
they do it a little farther and faster.

Trust me on this one.

